## 8. Security / authorization

- Method annotation on `addOwner` (controller line 129): `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")`, where `@roles` is the Spring bean `Roles` (`/home/daniel/.../security/Roles.java`) exposing `OWNER_ADMIN = "ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN"`. So an authenticated user needs `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`.
- **This is only enforced when method security is active.** `@EnableMethodSecurity(prePostEnabled = true)` lives on `BasicAuthenticationConfig` (`/home/daniel/.../security/BasicAuthenticationConfig.java`), which is `@ConditionalOnProperty(petclinic.security.enable=true)`. The default (`application.properties:49`) is `petclinic.security.enable=false`, activating `DisableSecurityConfig` (`permitAll`, CSRF disabled) — so **by default the endpoint is open and `@PreAuthorize` is not evaluated**.
- When enabled: HTTP Basic auth, CSRF disabled, users/roles loaded via JDBC from `users`/`roles` tables, passwords `BCryptPasswordEncoder`. No `@Secured`/servlet filters specific to this endpoint beyond the standard security chain. `@CrossOrigin(exposedHeaders = "errors, content-type")` is set at the controller class level.

